mkkitfs -- the session's FUSE server for Ribbon kit files (docs/MKKITFS.md in the Ribbon tree).

  src/          mkkitfs, in C++: the kit reader (kit.cpp, KIT-FORMAT.md section 11), the FUSE
                data path (server.cpp: libfuse low-level API, multithreaded, a bounded cache of
                hash-checked chunks), the command-line tools (main.cpp), and the confinement every
                command parses kits in (confine.cpp: seccomp allowlist, Landlock, no_new_privs, and
                the server's unmount guard); kit-swapmount (swapmount.c, C), ribbon-kit's live
                switch of the merged /usr view
  tcl/          mkkitfsd, the session server in Tcl (control socket, references, linger, idle
                exit, configuration, trust policy), and the Tcl package mkkitfs (the client
                `kit run` uses, and mkkitfs::compose for bubblewrap)
  tests/        tests/run.sh and what it runs: golden kits, damaged kits, confine-test.cpp, fuzz.py, fuse.tcl,
                trust.tcl, reads.py (concurrent reads, benchmark), startup.tcl, compose.tcl,
                alternatives.sh (extract, erofs, squashfuse), allocs.c (allocation counter)
  services/     the dinit user service mkkitfs (/usr/lib/dinit.d/user/mkkitfs)

Build: make METAKIT=<the Metakit fork, branch kit-fixes> [O=builddir]
Needs libfuse3, libdeflate, libcrypto (OpenSSL), a C++17 compiler; at run time Tcl with
unix_sockets, and fusermount3 for an unprivileged mount.
